// CAN Node ID of the application, used for filtering incoming CAN frames and setting the "from" address in ACK & NACK outgoing frames.
// Would be nicer to set this via some provided interface, but applications "might" crash if they try calling an interface
// During their startup function. So instead we use extern as a workaround.
extern uint8_t iMyNodeId;

// In CAN the top first 29 bits of the first four bytes are the CAN-ID.
// Bit 29 determines if CAN-ID is 11-bit (standard) or 29-bit (extended)
static const uint32_t iIsIdExtendedMask = 0x20000000u;

// The driver should be configured with address=application-control-can-id, so then
// the driver requires first four bytes for Can-ID and the rest of data is actual data of can frame
